.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-config 1  "config 0.3.0-beta.7"
.SH NAME
ag\-config \- Show, get, set and locate configuration (the user file; the repository\*(Aqs settings are shown read\-only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag config\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show, get, set and locate configuration (the user file; the repository\*(Aqs settings are shown read\-only)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ag\-config\-list(1)
Show every setting with its effective value and where it comes from
.TP
ag\-config\-get(1)
Print one setting\*(Aqs effective value (see `list` for the keys)
.TP
ag\-config\-set(1)
Store a user\-level setting: `identity` or `color`
.TP
ag\-config\-unset(1)
Remove a stored user\-level setting
.TP
ag\-config\-path(1)
Print the locations of the configuration files
.SH EXTRA
Files, environment variables and precedence: ag help config
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.7
